  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, thanks for reporting this. I checked your account and it is active with no sign-in problems. Your desktop (BL-DT-0108) is currently showing as offline, so it may be powered off or not connected. Please do the following and let us know the results: 1) Make sure your desktop is on and connected to the network, then fully close and reopen Outlook. 2) Check whether the orders@ mailbox shows up in Outlook on the web (click Add shared folder or mailbox and enter orders@). 3) Tell us whether you are working on BL-DT-0108 or a different computer. If orders@ still does not appear after a restart, reply to this ticket and we will confirm whether your access to the shared mailbox was granted. If it was not, the mailbox owner will need to approve the request before we can add it.",
  "internal_note": "Sender James O'Connor (user_id 8, Operations, Warehouse Supervisor, America/Chicago, usual hours 06:00-14:00). Account active, not blocked, 0 failed logins, password set 2026-09-11, mailbox 29.7% used (no quota issue). Assigned device BL-DT-0108 (Win11 desktop) shows offline, last check-in 2026-10-11 01:04 UTC (about 20:04 CDT the prior evening, outside usual hours), disk 78% free, no warnings. Cannot verify shared-mailbox permission grant with available tools. Per KB-011: next steps are user restart Outlook, check OWA, and manual add if needed. If the user was never granted access, KB-011 says mailbox owner approval is required, then Tier 2 makes the change (KB-006 referenced in article, not provided). Not a sending-as issue reported. No actions queued. Follow up: confirm device is on, confirm user's OWA result, verify orders@ access grant.",
